   1:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c **** /**
   2:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****   ******************************************************************************
   3:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****   * @file    stm32f4xx_hash.c
   4:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****   * @author  MCD Application Team
   5:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****   * @version V1.8.0
   6:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****   * @date    04-November-2016
   7:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****   * @brief   This file provides firmware functions to manage the following 
   8:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****   *          functionalities of the HASH / HMAC Processor (HASH) peripheral:           
   9:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****   *           - Initialization and Configuration functions
  10:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****   *           - Message Digest generation functions
  11:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****   *           - context swapping functions   
  12:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****   *           - DMA interface function       
  13:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****   *           - Interrupts and flags management       
  14:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****   *         
  15:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c **** @verbatim
  16:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****  ===================================================================      
  17:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****                  ##### How to use this driver #####
  18:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****  ===================================================================
  19:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****             
  20:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****  *** HASH operation : *** 
  21:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****  ========================                 
  22:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****  [..]
  23:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****    (#) Enable the HASH controller clock using 
  24:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****        RCC_AHB2PeriphClockCmd(RCC_AHB2Periph_HASH, ENABLE) function.
  25:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****              
  26:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****    (#) Initialize the HASH using HASH_Init() function. 
  27:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****                  
  28:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****    (#) Reset the HASH processor core, so that the HASH will be ready 
  29:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****        to compute he message digest of a new message by using HASH_Reset() function.
  30:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****   
ARM GAS  /tmp/ccfaT0jo.s 			page 2


  31:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****    (#) Enable the HASH controller using the HASH_Cmd() function. 
  32:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****                   
  33:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****    (#) if using DMA for Data input transfer, Activate the DMA Request 
  34:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****        using HASH_DMACmd() function 
  35:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****                       
  36:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****    (#) if DMA is not used for data transfer, use HASH_DataIn() function 
  37:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****        to enter data to IN FIFO.
  38:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****                
  39:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****             
  40:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****    (#) Configure the Number of valid bits in last word of the message 
  41:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****        using HASH_SetLastWordValidBitsNbr() function.
  42:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****                
  43:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****    (#) if the message length is not an exact multiple of 512 bits, 
  44:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****        then the function HASH_StartDigest() must be called to launch the computation
  45:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****        of the final digest.     
  46:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****                
  47:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****    (#) Once computed, the digest can be read using HASH_GetDigest() function.         
  48:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****                      
  49:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****    (#) To control HASH events you can use one of the following wo methods:
  50:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****        (++) Check on HASH flags using the HASH_GetFlagStatus() function.  
  51:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****        (++) Use HASH interrupts through the function HASH_ITConfig() at 
  52:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****             initialization phase and HASH_GetITStatus() function into 
  53:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****             interrupt routines in hashing phase.
  54:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****             After checking on a flag you should clear it using HASH_ClearFlag()
  55:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****             function. And after checking on an interrupt event you should 
  56:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****             clear it using HASH_ClearITPendingBit() function.     
  57:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****                        
  58:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****    (#) Save and restore hash processor context using 
  59:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****        HASH_SaveContext() and HASH_RestoreContext() functions.     
  60:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****                 
  61:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****   
  62:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****               
  63:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****  *** HMAC operation : *** 
  64:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****  ========================
  65:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****  [..] The HMAC algorithm is used for message authentication, by 
  66:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****       irreversibly binding the message being processed to a key chosen 
  67:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****       by the user. 
  68:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****       For HMAC specifications, refer to "HMAC: keyed-hashing for message 
  69:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****       authentication, H. Krawczyk, M. Bellare, R. Canetti, February 1997"
  70:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****             
  71:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****  [..] Basically, the HMAC algorithm consists of two nested hash operations:
  72:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****       HMAC(message) = Hash[((key | pad) XOR 0x5C) | Hash(((key | pad) XOR 0x36) | message)]
  73:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****       where:
  74:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****       (+) "pad" is a sequence of zeroes needed to extend the key to the 
  75:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****           length of the underlying hash function data block (that is 
  76:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****           512 bits for both the SHA-1 and MD5 hash algorithms)
  77:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****       (+) "|"   represents the concatenation operator 
  78:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****             
  79:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****            
  80:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****  [..]To compute the HMAC, four different phases are required:                  
  81:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****    (#) Initialize the HASH using HASH_Init() function to do HMAC 
  82:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****        operation. 
  83:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****                   
  84:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****    (#) The key (to be used for the inner hash function) is then given to the core. 
  85:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****        This operation follows the same mechanism as the one used to send the 
  86:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****        message in the hash operation (that is, by HASH_DataIn() function and, 
  87:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****        finally, HASH_StartDigest() function.
ARM GAS  /tmp/ccfaT0jo.s 			page 3


  88:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****             
  89:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****    (#) Once the last word has been entered and computation has started, 
  90:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****        the hash processor elaborates the key. It is then ready to accept the message
  91:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****        text using the same mechanism as the one used to send the message in the
  92:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****        hash operation.
  93:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****          
  94:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****    (#) After the first hash round, the hash processor returns "ready" to indicate 
  95:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****        that it is ready to receive the key to be used for the outer hash function 
  96:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****        (normally, this key is the same as the one used for the inner hash function). 
  97:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****        When the last word of the key is entered and computation starts, the HMAC 
  98:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****        result is made available using HASH_GetDigest() function.
  99:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c **** 
 100:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c **** @endverbatim
