 366:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****  ===============================================================================
 367:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****                       ##### Context swapping functions #####
 368:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****  ===============================================================================  
 369:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****  
 370:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****  [..] This section provides functions allowing to save and store HASH Context
 371:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****   
 372:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****  [..] It is possible to interrupt a HASH/HMAC process to perform another processing 
 373:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****       with a higher priority, and to complete the interrupted process later on, when 
 374:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****       the higher priority task is complete. To do so, the context of the interrupted 
 375:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****       task must be saved from the HASH registers to memory, and then be restored 
 376:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****       from memory to the HASH registers.
 377:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****   
 378:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****    (#) To save the current context, use HASH_SaveContext() function
 379:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****    (#) To restore the saved context, use HASH_RestoreContext() function 
 380:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****   
 381:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c **** 
 382:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c **** @endverbatim
 383:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****   * @{
 384:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****   */
 385:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****   
 386:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c **** /**
 387:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****   * @brief  Save the Hash peripheral Context. 
 388:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****   * @note   The context can be saved only when no block is currently being 
 389:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****   *         processed. So user must wait for DINIS = 1 (the last block has been 
 390:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****   *         processed and the input FIFO is empty) or NBW != 0 (the FIFO is not 
 391:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****   *         full and no processing is ongoing).   
 392:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****   * @param  HASH_ContextSave: pointer to a HASH_Context structure that contains
 393:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****   *         the repository for current context.
 394:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****   * @retval None
 395:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****   */
