 509:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c **** /** @defgroup HASH_Group5 Interrupts and flags management functions
 510:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****  *  @brief   Interrupts and flags management functions
ARM GAS  /tmp/ccfaT0jo.s 			page 21


 511:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****  *
 512:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c **** @verbatim   
 513:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****  ===============================================================================
 514:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****                ##### Interrupts and flags management functions #####
 515:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****  ===============================================================================  
 516:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c **** 
 517:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****  [..] This section provides functions allowing to configure the HASH Interrupts and 
 518:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****       to get the status and clear flags and Interrupts pending bits.
 519:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****   
 520:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****  [..] The HASH provides 2 Interrupts sources and 5 Flags:
 521:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****   
 522:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****  *** Flags : ***
 523:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****  =============== 
 524:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****  [..]
 525:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****    (#) HASH_FLAG_DINIS : set when 16 locations are free in the Data IN FIFO 
 526:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****       which means that a  new block (512 bit) can be entered into the input buffer.
 527:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****                           
 528:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****    (#) HASH_FLAG_DCIS :  set when Digest calculation is complete
 529:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****       
 530:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****    (#) HASH_FLAG_DMAS :  set when HASH's DMA interface is enabled (DMAE=1) or 
 531:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****        a transfer is ongoing. This Flag is cleared only by hardware.
 532:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****                            
 533:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****    (#) HASH_FLAG_BUSY :  set when The hash core is processing a block of data
 534:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****        This Flag is cleared only by hardware. 
 535:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****                            
 536:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****    (#) HASH_FLAG_DINNE : set when Data IN FIFO is not empty which means that 
 537:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****        the Data IN FIFO contains at least one word of data. This Flag is cleared 
 538:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****        only by hardware.
 539:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****      
 540:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****  *** Interrupts : ***
 541:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****  ====================
 542:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****  [..]   
 543:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****    (#) HASH_IT_DINI  : if enabled, this interrupt source is pending when 16 
 544:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****        locations are free in the Data IN FIFO  which means that a new block (512 bit)
 545:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****        can be entered into the input buffer. This interrupt source is cleared using 
 546:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****        HASH_ClearITPendingBit(HASH_IT_DINI) function.
 547:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****    
 548:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****    (#) HASH_IT_DCI   : if enabled, this interrupt source is pending when Digest 
 549:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****        calculation is complete. This interrupt source is cleared using 
 550:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****        HASH_ClearITPendingBit(HASH_IT_DCI) function.
 551:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c **** 
 552:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****  *** Managing the HASH controller events : ***
 553:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****  =============================================
 554:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****  [..] The user should identify which mode will be used in his application to manage 
 555:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****       the HASH controller events: Polling mode or Interrupt mode.
 556:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****   
 557:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****    (#) In the Polling Mode it is advised to use the following functions:
 558:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****        (++) HASH_GetFlagStatus() : to check if flags events occur. 
 559:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****        (++) HASH_ClearFlag()     : to clear the flags events.
 560:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****     
 561:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****    (#)  In the Interrupt Mode it is advised to use the following functions:
 562:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****        (++) HASH_ITConfig()       : to enable or disable the interrupt source.
 563:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****        (++) HASH_GetITStatus()    : to check if Interrupt occurs.
 564:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****        (++) HASH_ClearITPendingBit() : to clear the Interrupt pending Bit 
 565:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****             (corresponding Flag). 
 566:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c **** 
 567:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c **** @endverbatim
ARM GAS  /tmp/ccfaT0jo.s 			page 22


 568:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****   * @{
 569:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_hash.c ****   */ 
